WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:05.360
And now, before we deep dive into the 30 best practices, I'm going to give you the golden rule.

00:05.360 --> 00:09.400
The SQL optimizer responds differently for different sizes of tables.

00:09.400 --> 00:14.320
So that means if you have small and medium tables like hundreds of thousands, you might not notice

00:14.320 --> 00:17.440
any performance differences if you are following the best practices.

00:17.440 --> 00:19.600
And that's because the size of the data is small.

00:19.600 --> 00:25.160
But if you have like million or hundreds of millions of records in tables, you will immediately notice

00:25.160 --> 00:28.280
how things can be faster if you follow the best practices.

00:28.280 --> 00:33.280
And here is my golden rule if you get any best practice from me, or let's say you are reading something

00:33.280 --> 00:37.200
in the internet, always you have to test using the execution plan.

00:37.240 --> 00:41.840
So for example, if you have like two queries are returning the same result of the data, I'm going

00:41.880 --> 00:44.280
to recommend you here to check the execution plan.

00:44.280 --> 00:49.480
And if you noticed, there is no differences between them in the execution plan, then pick the one

00:49.480 --> 00:50.240
that you see.

00:50.240 --> 00:55.200
It is easier to read and to understand because sometimes if you are following the best practices for

00:55.200 --> 00:59.200
the performance, your query might be like a little bit more complicated.

00:59.200 --> 01:04.760
So always write the query to be understandable and only optimize it if you notice it is slow.

01:04.760 --> 01:07.680
So the golden rule here is always test.

01:07.680 --> 01:13.440
If you find you are optimizing the performance with the new query, then pick that and if there is no

01:13.440 --> 01:17.200
gain in the performance, then focus on making your queries readable.

01:17.200 --> 01:18.520
So this is the golden rule.

01:18.520 --> 01:21.160
Always test test test using execution plan.

01:21.200 --> 01:23.520
So let's deep dive into best practices.

01:23.520 --> 01:27.200
And we're going to start by optimizing the performance of our queries.
